ated status surface never a session input.\"\nrationale = \"\"\"Realizes SN-006 and the dissolved edge expectation that an unattended run never blocks on a prompt, at launch or mid-run. The acceptance is deliberately narrower than it once was: it had carried two obligations the shall never stated - transient-limit backoff and stall abort - and an acceptance cell cannot mint a requirement. Both were MINTED rather than deleted, because each describes live behaviour worth keeping: SR-171 and SR-172. An unattended run blocked on a prompt is indistinguishable from a hung one and holds its lane until a human notices. Keeping a separate serial resume path beside the dispatcher was rejected: two authorities over one decision drift, and the divergence surfaces as a run that resumes differently depending on how it was started.\"\"\"\nacceptance_criteria = \"A worker reconciles from its assignment + committed evidence and the integrator from trunk history; every mode runs with stdin closed and a prompt cannot wedge it.\"\npriority = \"S\"\nverification = \"Test\"\nstatus = \"Approved\"\nphase = 1\nda_refs = [\"DA-006\", \"DA-008\"]","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"62488e29-4f8f-46dc-a1ab-0647d367ffcd","uuid":"eb3d0e9d-e5a4-4ae6-a822-c8d40be4d835","timestamp":"2026-11-07T22:07:01.115Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"?? docs/reviews/wi-1002/003-ADJUDICATE-8e5e544.md\n?? docs/reviews/wi-1002/003-ADJUDICATE-8e5e544.md.requested\n8e5e5441b WI-1002: checkpoint reconcile: TC-137's added sentence names the run as the claimant and states the no-stall and ruled-item halves (Terra, by addition; LLR-143 confirmed unchanged), the stray pytest import leaves the stub check string, and round 1's triage is recorded (D-002)\ne74ab1107 telemetry: session 33ad6778484948cbbff4c8bb9ff13229 AUTHOR COMPLETED\n3d7cce78b WI-1002: review round 1 at c873dcf: REVIEW-A (Codex Sol, medium) APPROVE with no findings, REVIEW-B (Claude Opus high stand-in) APPROVE with three MINORs\n257